  "Poet and novelist; one of the most popular poets of the 1860s and the author of 'The High Tide on the Coast of Lincolnshire'.",
  "Born in Boston, Lincolnshire, on 17 March 1820; she published Poems in 1863 and sold 20,000 copies in a few months, followed by A Story of Doom (1867), Mopsa the Fairy (1869) and Off the Skelligs (1872). She was one of the most popular poets of the mid-Victorian period and died in Kensington on 20 July 1897.",
  "Jean Ingelow was one of the most popular poets of the 1860s and her 'The High Tide on the Coast of Lincolnshire' is one of the best-loved English narrative poems of the century: her ballad of the fenland flood and her children's fantasy Mopsa the Fairy gave the period two of its permanent favourites.",
